hs ago; Crawled: yesterday; Form January 1, 2026 ... PDF Form\n\nForm January 1, 2026\n\n# Preliminary Orders After Request for Relief Under the Racial Justice Act—Juvenile Adjudication\n\nPDF Form\n\nDownload PDF--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRules Committee Meeting_December 4_2025 (https://courts.ca.gov/system/files/file/rules-20251204-materials.pdf)\nciteturn2020search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10 months ago; Crawled: 10 months ago; https://courts.ca.gov/policy-administration/invitations-comment ... <tr><td>Adopt forms EJ-200, EJ-202, and EJ-205; revise forms EJ-130, EJ-150, WG-002, WG-003, WG-004, WG-005, WG-015/EJ-135, WG-017/EJ-137, WG-022, and WG-030</td><td>July 1, 2026</td></tr> ... These form revisions fall into two categories: revisions that are being recommended to the Judicial Council for approval effective January 1, 2026 (these revisions are highlighted in green in the draft forms attached to this invitation to comment), and revisions that will be recommended with an effective date of July 1, 2026 (these proposed revisions are highlighted in yellow in the draft forms).\nJudicial Council of California  \n455 Golden Gate Avenue · San Francisco, California 94102-3688  \nhttps://courts.ca.gov/policy-administration/invitations-comment\n\nINVITATION TO COMMENT  \nW26-02\n\n<table id=\"e1\">\n<tr><td><b>Title</b></td><td><b>Action Requested</b></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Civil Practice and Procedure: Revisions to Enforcement of Judgment and Wage Garnishment Forms to Implement Assembly Bill 774</td><td>Review and submit comments by January 7, 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Proposed Rules, Forms, Standards, or Statutes</b></td><td><b>Proposed Effective Date</b></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Adopt forms EJ-200, EJ-202, and EJ-205; revise forms EJ-130, EJ-150, WG-002, WG-003, WG-004, WG-005, WG-015/EJ-135, WG-017/EJ-137, WG-022, and WG-030</td><td>July 1, 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td><b>Proposed by</b></td><td><b>Contact</b></td></tr>\n<tr><td>Civil and Small Claims Advisory Committee<br>Hon. Samantha P. Jessner, Chair</td><td>Jenny Grantz, 415-865-4394<br>jenny.grantz@jud.ca.gov</td></tr>\n</table>\n\nExecutive Summary and Origin\n\nAssembly Bill 774 (Stats. 2025, ch. 708), makes several changes to the laws regarding enforcement of judgment, including creation of a new procedure by which the judgment creditor may seek reinstatement of a judgment lien on real or personal property. The Civil and Small Claims Advisory Committee proposes adopting 3 forms and revising 10 forms to implement AB 774.\n\nThe Proposal\n\nThe Civil and Small Claims Advisory Committee proposes adopting 3 forms and revising 10 forms to implement AB 774. These form revisions fall into two categories: revisions that are being recommended to the Judicial Council for approval effective January 1, 2026 (these revisions are highlighted in green in the draft forms attached to this invitation to comment), and revisions that will be recommended with an effective date of July 1, 2026 (these proposed revisions are highlighted in yellow in the draft forms). This dual structure is needed because\n\nThis proposal has not been approved by the Judicial Council and is not intended to represent the views of the council, its Rules Committee, or its Legislation Committee. It is circulated for comment purposes only.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n| California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/find-forms?page=0&query=JUD-)\nciteturn2020search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today;   * EJ-115 * Notice of Application for Recognition and Entry of Tribal Court Money Judgment Effective: July 1, 2015 ...   * WG-002 * Earnings Withholding Order Effective: January 1, 2026 汉语 한국어 español Tiếng Việt\n  * WG-002 * Earnings Withholding Order Effective: January 1, 2026 汉语 한국어 español Tiếng Việt\n\nSee form info Download\n\n  * WG-003 * Employee Instructions Effective: January 1, 2026 汉语 한국어